How the EA Works
1. Initialization (OnInit)
Validates all inputs (periods, lot, hours, max positions).
Creates two iMA handles (fast and slow EMA) on the selected timeframe.
Configures the CTrade object with the magic number, deviation, filling mode, and logs only errors.

2.Per-bar processing (OnTick)
On every tick it checks SERIES_LASTBAR_DATE. If a new bar has not opened, it returns immediately.
When a new bar opens, the previous bar is now "completed", so crossover logic runs exactly once per bar.

3.Crossover detection (UpdateCrossoverState)
Copies the last two completed candles (shift 1 and shift 2) for both EMAs using CopyBuffer.
Bullish cross condition: fast[1] <= slow[1] and fast[0] > slow[0].
A new cross sets g_bullishCrossDetected = true and re-arms g_tradePlacedForCross = false.

4.Entry gating
A BUY is attempted only if:
A new bullish cross was detected and not yet traded (!g_tradePlacedForCross).
Current server time is within trading hours.
Current server weekday is enabled.
Open EA positions count < InpMaxPositions.
No existing EA position for this symbol/magic (HasNoOpenPosition).

5.Trade execution (TryOpenBuy)
Validates the tick, converts pips to price using quote precision, and checks broker stops level.
Normalizes lot to min/max/step, checks free margin with OrderCalcMargin.
Computes SL/TP relative to the actual ask price (BUY entry) and normalizes to tick size.
Calls trade.Buy(...) and logs the result code on failure.

6.Duplicate prevention
g_tradePlacedForCross is set true once a trade is placed for a cross and is only reset when a new bullish cross is detected. Combined with the "one position per magic/symbol" check, this prevents re-entry on the same cross.

7.Bearish crosses
No SELL is opened. No BUY is closed. Existing BUYs are left to hit SL/TP.

8.Cleanup (OnDeinit)
Releases both indicator handles with IndicatorRelease.

