4. Installation in MetaTrader 5
Open MetaTrader 5.
Menu File → Open Data Folder.
Navigate to MQL5\Experts\.
Create a folder (e.g., EMACrossover) and save the file as EMA_Crossover_EA.mq5 inside it.
Restart MT5 or right-click in the Navigator panel and choose Refresh.
The EA will appear under Navigator → Expert Advisors.

5. Compiling & Backtesting
Compile
In MT5, press F4 to open MetaEditor.
Open EMA_Crossover_EA.mq5.
Press F7 (Compile). Confirm zero errors and zero warnings.
The compiled .ex5 appears next to the source.

Backtest
In MT5, press Ctrl+R to open the Strategy Tester.
Select Expert: EMA_Crossover_EA.
Select Symbol: e.g., EURUSD.
Select Period: H1 (or your preferred timeframe).
Select Model: "Every tick based on real ticks" for realistic execution, or "1 minute OHLC" for faster runs.
Set the date range, initial deposit, and leverage.
Ensure Use broker server time is enabled so trading-hour filters work correctly.
Click Start. Review the Journal and Trade tabs for execution logs, error retcodes, and SL/TP placement.

6. Limitations & Assumptions
One symbol per chart: The EA is designed to run on a single symbol chart. The "one position per symbol/magic" check makes it safe if attached to multiple charts of the same symbol, but you should use distinct magic numbers per chart if you want independent control.
Per-bar entry only: Crossovers are evaluated once per new bar. A cross that occurs and then reverses within the same bar will still trigger the entry on bar close of the next bar only if the condition holds on completed data. This is intentional and matches the "completed candles only" requirement.
Pip conversion: Assumes standard FX conventions (3/5-digit → 10 points per pip; otherwise 1 point per pip). Exotic instruments with unusual tick sizes may need adjustment.
Broker stops level: Some brokers return SYMBOL_TRADE_STOPS_LEVEL = 0, in which case a spread-based fallback is used. Always verify on your broker.
Filling mode: SetTypeFillingBySymbol picks a broker-supported filling type; if a broker requires a specific mode, the trade may still fail with retcode 10030 — check the log.
No trailing stop / break-even: Not part of this initial version; SL/TP are static until closed.
Bearish crosses: Ignored by design (no SELL, no forced close of BUY).
Slippage: Deviation is fixed at 10 points; not exposed as an input in this version.
Max positions: Although InpMaxPositions exists, duplicate prevention (HasNoOpenPosition) effectively limits the EA to one position per symbol per magic. Raise this only if you later modify the duplicate-prevention logic.
Server time: Trading hours use TimeCurrent() (broker server time), exactly as required.
Backtest realism: Results depend heavily on the model chosen; use "Every tick based on real ticks" for realistic spread/SL/TP behavior.
Margin check: OrderCalcMargin is used pre-trade; if it fails on exotic symbols, the trade is skipped.
